Exponentially synchronization of coupled exosystems
Noticing that the coupled exosystem \eqref{II02} is independent of the agent dynamics, the closed-loop systems \eqref{II05} and \eqref{II07} can be regarded as to be driven by an lumped exosystem $w$ of $Ns$ dimensions. Since the lumped exosystem has the dimension in excess of what is required, its dynamics must contain some decay modes, that is, in some vector directions $w$ is asymptotically converging to zeros. In order for the second condition 1b) or 2b), the undecayed mode must be the flow determined by the vector field $s(w_0)$, which means that all the exosystems should synchronize. To this end, the following result is recalled (Corollary 7 in \cite{XiangIJC2011}),
and rephrased as follows,
\begin{lemma} \label{le01}
Given a multi-agent system \eqref{II02} with communication graph $\mathcal{G}_{\sigma(t)}$satisfying assumption A4). If the largest Lyapunov exponent $\nu_{max}$ of system $\dot{w}_0=s(w_0)$ and the consensus convergence rate $\alpha^*(T,t)$ of $\mathcal{G}_{\sigma(t)}$ are such that
\begin{equation}
  \label{III01}
  \nu_{max}+\ln(\alpha^*(T,t))/T<0
\end{equation}
then system \eqref{II02} is locally exponentially synchronizable.
\end{lemma}

