\begin{equation}
  \nu_{max} = \lim_{t\rightarrow \infty} \lim_{\delta w^0\rightarrow 0}\frac{1}{t} \ln\frac{\|\Phi_t^s(w^0+\delta w^0)-\Phi_t^s(w^0)\|}{\|\delta w^0\|}
\end{equation}

On the other hand, consider the consensus rate of a switching graph. Define the time interval sequence $\{\delta_k\}$ by $\delta_k = t_k-t_{k-1}$, $k=1,2,\cdots$. Let $t^1$ and $t^2$ be two time instants located in the time slots of $[t_{i-1}, t_i)$ and $[t_{j-1},t_j)$ with $i\le j$, respectively.

