On the other hand, with assumption A1), $\nu_{max}\le 0$. If not, for any given $\epsilon$, there is a time $T_\epsilon$, such that for any $0<\|\delta w^0\|<\epsilon$, $\|\Phi_t^s(w^0+\delta w^0)\|>\epsilon$ for all $t>T_\epsilon$. This is contradictory to the feature of Poisson stable \cite{IsidoriTAC1990}.

