consensus convergent rate is defined as the supremum of the contract rate of transition matrix $\Phi(t+(k-1)T,t+kT)$ \cite{XiangIJC2011},
\begin{equation}
  \alpha^*(T,t)=\sup_k \alpha(\Phi(t+(k-1)T,t+kT))
\end{equation}
